# Test before push

CapRover deploys only after GitHub Actions goes green. Pushing untested main commits has already blocked deploy twice.

**Before `git push` (or any commit the user asked to push):**

1. Run the same suite CI runs, in order:
   - `npm test`
   - `npm run test:integration`
   - `npm run test:e2e`
2. Fix failures locally. Do not push hoping CI will catch them.
3. Only push after all three succeed.

`npm test` alone is not enough — e2e is what usually fails after plan/editor UX changes. Rebuild before e2e when client code changed (`npm run test:e2e` already builds).
